# Everything under state/ is live runtime, and NOTHING here is source.
#
# Ignore-by-default rather than enumerating subdirectories. The root .gitignore
# used to list them one at a time (state/logs/, state/worktrees/,
# state/improvements/, …), which meant every NEW runtime directory arrived
# untracked and stayed one `git add -A` away from being committed. That is how
# `state/idle_ping/` showed up in `git status` after the idle-ping feature
# shipped: nobody remembered to add a rule, and the rule set had no way to
# notice.
#
# A denylist you must remember to extend is not a guardrail. This inverts it —
# a new runtime path is ignored the moment it is written, with no maintenance —
# and it matches what CLAUDE.md already promises: "state/** is runtime and
# gitignored. Never `git add -A` here."
#
# If something under state/ ever genuinely needs tracking, allowlist that exact
# path below with a `!` rule, so the exception is deliberate and reviewable.
*
!.gitignore
